WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.265 --> 00:00:01.140
SOWMYA KANNAN: Hello.

00:00:01.140 --> 00:00:05.000
Welcome to the Google Cloud
career readiness program.

00:00:05.000 --> 00:00:08.930
Google Cloud has developed a
cloud engineer career readiness

00:00:08.930 --> 00:00:13.390
path for students and
faculty in higher education.

00:00:13.390 --> 00:00:16.000
Let's take a look at
the cloud landscape

00:00:16.000 --> 00:00:20.890
and learn more about the
Associate Cloud Engineer Track.

00:00:20.890 --> 00:00:23.500
Enterprises are
migrating to the cloud

00:00:23.500 --> 00:00:26.560
and building new
applications on the cloud.

00:00:26.560 --> 00:00:30.340
Leading industry research
indicates that a shift to cloud

00:00:30.340 --> 00:00:35.700
will affect more than $1
trillion in IT spending.

00:00:35.700 --> 00:00:38.100
Adoption of cloud-native
applications

00:00:38.100 --> 00:00:40.880
will double by 2020.

00:00:40.880 --> 00:00:43.550
This accelerated
move towards cloud

00:00:43.550 --> 00:00:47.300
has created a tremendous demand
for qualified professionals,

00:00:47.300 --> 00:00:49.970
who are proficient in
cloud technologies.

00:00:49.970 --> 00:00:53.490
Traditional roles are evolving
in a cloud-first world.

00:00:53.490 --> 00:00:56.960
For example, an app
developer or data analyst

00:00:56.960 --> 00:01:01.470
needs new skills to succeed
with cloud technologies.

00:01:01.470 --> 00:01:04.400
New roles related to
DevOps, data science,

00:01:04.400 --> 00:01:06.660
and machine learning
are emerging.

00:01:06.660 --> 00:01:10.940
You can kickstart your career
in cloud-related career paths.

00:01:10.940 --> 00:01:14.210
Google's leading edge,
enterprise-ready curriculum

00:01:14.210 --> 00:01:16.700
and learning
resources can help you

00:01:16.700 --> 00:01:20.270
achieve industry-recognized
Associate Cloud Engineer

00:01:20.270 --> 00:01:21.890
certification.

00:01:21.890 --> 00:01:23.660
The Associate Cloud
Engineer Track

00:01:23.660 --> 00:01:26.150
provides training free
of charge to prepare

00:01:26.150 --> 00:01:30.830
for the Associate Cloud
Engineer certification exam.

00:01:30.830 --> 00:01:33.820
This track includes
access to the Architecting

00:01:33.820 --> 00:01:38.290
with Google Cloud Platform
specialization on Coursera.

00:01:38.290 --> 00:01:42.190
This on-demand training
includes six in-depth courses,

00:01:42.190 --> 00:01:46.220
with videos, hands-on
labs, and quizzes.

00:01:46.220 --> 00:01:49.910
Hands-on experience
is crucial for success

00:01:49.910 --> 00:01:53.900
with the Associate Cloud
Engineer certification exam.

00:01:53.900 --> 00:01:56.960
You'll receive credits to
complete self-based labs

00:01:56.960 --> 00:02:01.340
on the Qwiklabs
platform free of charge.

00:02:01.340 --> 00:02:03.800
This training puts you
on the path to success

00:02:03.800 --> 00:02:08.850
for achieving the Associate
Cloud Engineer certification.

00:02:08.850 --> 00:02:12.550
Based on course completion
timelines and other criteria,

00:02:12.550 --> 00:02:18.510
students receive a 50% discount
on the certification exam.

00:02:18.510 --> 00:02:20.520
Familiarity with
the following topics

00:02:20.520 --> 00:02:23.290
is helpful for success with
the Associate Cloud Engineer

00:02:23.290 --> 00:02:24.690
Track--

00:02:24.690 --> 00:02:29.490
operating systems, file systems,
the IP networking stack,

00:02:29.490 --> 00:02:32.820
how web browsers and
web servers communicate,

00:02:32.820 --> 00:02:37.650
databases, programming, working
with Linux at the command line,

00:02:37.650 --> 00:02:41.130
and editing text files from
the Linux command line.

00:02:41.130 --> 00:02:43.260
To participate in
this track, you'll

00:02:43.260 --> 00:02:47.100
need a laptop or desktop
with the latest versions

00:02:47.100 --> 00:02:49.380
of any popular web browser.

00:02:49.380 --> 00:02:51.960
The Google Chrome
browser is recommended.

00:02:51.960 --> 00:02:56.250
A robust internet connection
to access Google Cloud Platform

00:02:56.250 --> 00:02:59.900
console is required.

00:02:59.900 --> 00:03:03.560
Let's look at the training
in a bit more detail.

00:03:03.560 --> 00:03:05.450
The Associate Cloud
Engineer Track

00:03:05.450 --> 00:03:08.320
has two main
training components.

00:03:08.320 --> 00:03:11.600
The Architecting with Google
Cloud Platform specialization

00:03:11.600 --> 00:03:14.240
on Coursera covers
topics related

00:03:14.240 --> 00:03:18.090
to exploring and deploying
solution elements,

00:03:18.090 --> 00:03:19.910
including infrastructure
components,

00:03:19.910 --> 00:03:24.690
such as networks, systems,
and application services.

00:03:24.690 --> 00:03:28.030
The Cloud Architecture Quest
on the Qwiklabs platform

00:03:28.030 --> 00:03:31.210
is a set of hands-on labs
that provide practice

00:03:31.210 --> 00:03:34.900
on topics and services that
appear in the Associate Cloud

00:03:34.900 --> 00:03:37.710
Engineer certification exam.

00:03:37.710 --> 00:03:41.130
It's highly recommended that
you complete additional labs

00:03:41.130 --> 00:03:42.520
as well.

00:03:42.520 --> 00:03:45.520
The training you'll receive in
the Associate Cloud Engineer

00:03:45.520 --> 00:03:48.400
Track provides a
solid foundation

00:03:48.400 --> 00:03:51.890
for preparing to take
the certification exam.

00:03:51.890 --> 00:03:56.110
However, the training does
not teach exactly what

00:03:56.110 --> 00:03:58.490
you will need to pass the test.

00:03:58.490 --> 00:04:02.800
Practical hands-on
experience is also needed.

00:04:02.800 --> 00:04:05.950
Make sure to get hands-on
experience by practicing

00:04:05.950 --> 00:04:08.440
with the suggested
labs in Qwiklabs

00:04:08.440 --> 00:04:11.620
and to review product
documentation.

00:04:11.620 --> 00:04:15.760
You'll earn a course completion
certificate from Google Cloud

00:04:15.760 --> 00:04:20.519
upon completing the Coursera
specialization successfully.

00:04:20.519 --> 00:04:24.630
Success in the Associate Cloud
Engineer certification exam

00:04:24.630 --> 00:04:27.810
enables you to demonstrate
to potential employers

00:04:27.810 --> 00:04:30.480
that you have the skills
necessary to succeed

00:04:30.480 --> 00:04:33.030
in roles that
require proficiency

00:04:33.030 --> 00:04:35.890
in cloud technologies.

00:04:35.890 --> 00:04:37.720
The Associate Cloud
Engineer Track

00:04:37.720 --> 00:04:40.720
must be completed in 16 weeks.

00:04:40.720 --> 00:04:44.960
This slide shows a
suggested timeline.

00:04:44.960 --> 00:04:47.720
Complete Architecting
with Google Cloud Platform

00:04:47.720 --> 00:04:51.770
specialization within
the first 9 weeks.

00:04:51.770 --> 00:04:55.790
Complete Cloud Architecture
Quest and other hands-on labs

00:04:55.790 --> 00:04:58.350
by week 16.

00:04:58.350 --> 00:05:05.060
Your access to Coursera will
expire at the end of 16 weeks.

00:05:05.060 --> 00:05:07.460
Practice for the
certification exam,

00:05:07.460 --> 00:05:12.820
and complete the exam before
the voucher expiration date.

00:05:12.820 --> 00:05:17.430
Remember, you can race ahead
of the suggested timeline.

00:05:17.430 --> 00:05:22.060
Let's now take a quick look at
the Student Resource Center.

00:05:22.060 --> 00:05:25.790
The Student Resource Center
includes FAQs, as well as

00:05:25.790 --> 00:05:29.370
Study Jam materials
for extra practice.

00:05:29.370 --> 00:05:34.120
To clarify, Study Jams
are essentially workshops.

00:05:34.120 --> 00:05:37.680
If you're not able to meet other
students in a workshop setting,

00:05:37.680 --> 00:05:40.590
you can work through the Study
Jam materials on your own,

00:05:40.590 --> 00:05:41.770
as well.

00:05:41.770 --> 00:05:45.750
If you have questions about the
Associate Cloud Engineer Track,

00:05:45.750 --> 00:05:50.190
check the FAQs and the support
section for information.

00:05:50.190 --> 00:05:52.070
Happy learning.

